development.question_text:
The graph of $y=x^2$ is shown dashed. Sketch $y=x^2+2$ on the same axes and mark its vertex.
[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[every node/.style={font=\large}]
\begin{axis}[axis lines=middle, xlabel={$x$}, ylabel={$y$}, xmin=-4.5, xmax=4.5, ymin=-1, ymax=9, samples=100, clip=false, axis line style={-{Stealth}}, xtick={-4,-2,2,4}, ytick={2,4,6,8}]
\addplot[smooth, thick, dashed, domain=-3:3] {x*x};
\end{axis}
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]

development.solution_text:
$y=x^2+2$ is $y=x^2$ translated up $2$ units, so the vertex moves from $(0,0)$ to $(0,2)$.
[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[every node/.style={font=\large}]
\begin{axis}[axis lines=middle, xlabel={$x$}, ylabel={$y$}, xmin=-4.5, xmax=4.5, ymin=-1, ymax=9, samples=100, clip=false, axis line style={-{Stealth}}, xtick={-4,-2,2,4}, ytick={2,4,6,8}]
\addplot[smooth, thick, dashed, domain=-3:3] {x*x};
\addplot[smooth, thick, blue, <->, domain=-2.65:2.65] {x*x+2};
\node[above right] at (axis cs:0,2) {$(0,2)$};
\end{axis}
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]

